The mutation gate was switched on for api (services/api) in acme, but no GitHub Actions step for this component runs mutation testing for Python. Add the step for each language below, so every pull request reports a mutation score.

No GitHub Actions job is mapped to this component yet. Add a workflow under .github/workflows that runs its tests on pull requests and on pushes to the default branch, then add the steps below to it.

Use the test runner and build tool the component already uses; the notes below name the usual tool for each, not a required one. If CI already does this through a script the check did not recognise (an `npm test` script, a `make` target), say so in your hand-off and change nothing for that language.

---

### Python

- Run mutmut (`mutmut run`, then `mutmut results`) with its settings in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.mutmut]`) or `setup.cfg`; Cosmic Ray is the alternative when the project already uses it.
- Point it at the source package and the existing test command, and upload its results.

---

## Done when

- Each language above has a CI step that runs mutation testing and uploads the report as a workflow artifact, with the mutation score in the job summary (`$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`).
- Mutation testing is slow: on pull requests, limit the run to the changed code where the tool supports it, and run the full suite on a schedule or on pushes to the default branch.
- Do not make CI fail on a minimum score unless the repository already enforces one.
- The tool's configuration lives in the repository (its config file or the build file), so a developer runs the same command locally.
- A language above with no tests in this component is skipped and named in your hand-off; writing its first tests is a separate task.
- The existing CI jobs still pass.